{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>and he dips his foot in oil.</b> He used the language of immersion on account of the abundance of oil in the land of Asher; therefore he said 'his foot' and not 'his hand' — in the manner of what is written (Genesis 49:11), ״כבס ביין לבושו״ — he uses the language of washing in wine on account of the abundance of wine in the land of Judah, like a person who sets aside water and washes his garments in wine, to express the extremity of abundance. And so Jacob mentioned (ibid.) ״מאשר שמנה לחמו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:21.650447554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}